                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is a healthy return rate for footwear D2C?</h3>
                                        <p>20-30% is normal. Under 20% indicates strong sizing tech. Over 35% needs immediate intervention (fit tech, better size charts, exchange-first flow).</p>
                                        <h3>Should I offer half sizes?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes for anything above the entry price point. Skipping half sizes to reduce SKU complexity costs more in returns than it saves in inventory.</p>
                                        <h3>How much does virtual size finder cost?</h3>
                                        <p>ShoeSize.me / Nike Fit-style tools: $8K-30K/year. Custom AR sizing: $20K-80K one-time build.</p>
                                        <h3>Which is the best footwear category for a new D2C brand in 2026?</h3>
                                        <p>Sustainable / vegan footwear in USA / UK. Athleisure in India. Premium sneakers in UAE. Kids' footwear is under-served across all four.</p>
